# Testing Standards

Use **Vitest** as the test runner. Test files live next to the code they test with a `.test.ts` or `.test.tsx` suffix.

```
lib/music/notes.ts         → lib/music/notes.test.ts
hooks/useChordGenerator.ts → hooks/useChordGenerator.test.ts
```

## When tests are required

| Layer | Rule |
|---|---|
| `lib/music/` | Every exported function gets a test. These are pure functions — no excuses. |
| `lib/ai/` | Test prompt builders in `prompts.ts`. Mock the fetch in `openrouter.ts`. |
| `lib/midi/` | Test MIDI export output against known byte sequences. |
| `hooks/` | Test the happy path and error states. Mock API calls and Tone.js. |
| `store/` | Test state transitions — what changes when an action is dispatched. |
| `components/` | Only test non-trivial logic (e.g. playback state, disabled states). Skip snapshot tests. |

## When to update tests

- Changing a function signature → update the test immediately, in the same commit
- Adding a parameter → add a test case covering the new parameter
- Fixing a bug → add a regression test that would have caught it

## Test structure

```typescript
// one describe block per function or component
describe("parseChordProgression", () => {
    it("returns chords in order", () => { ... })
    it("throws on invalid input", () => { ... })
})
```

## What not to test

- shadcn primitives in `components/ui/` — never modified, never tested here
- `app/layout.tsx` and `app/page.tsx` — pure composition, no logic
- CSS or Tailwind class names
